{"t": 1795069510.440195, "kind": "assistant", "text": "Dev was upgraded, but the compatibility check failed:\n\n- **Fresh dev snapshot:** `dev/pre-php-8.3-upgrade.tgz`\n- **Dev PHP:** upgraded from **8.1.34** to **8.3.31**\n- **Home page (`/`):** **HTTP 500 — PHP fatal error**\n- **Plugin named in the error:** `limit-login-attempts-reloaded` **3.4.4** (active)\n\nThis indicates a plugin incompatibility, so I stopped as required and did not deactivate or modify the plugin. **Production remains unchanged on PHP 8.1.34**, and I am not proposing a production PHP 8.3 deployment until this fatal error is investigated and resolved."}
